98581560284"><custom-block s="housekeeping"></custom-block><custom-block s="tree 1, size: %n"><l>50</l><comment w="515" collapsed="false">7.1.1.2 Due to the housekeeping block, the sprite starts at the origin facing up. TREE 1 leaves it in the same&#xD;state: at the origin facing up.</comment></custom-block></script><script x="13.333333333333382" y="58.75886524822707"><custom-block s="housekeeping"></custom-block><custom-block s="tree 2, size: %n"><l>50</l><comment w="90" collapsed="true">7.1.1.3</comment></custom-block></script><script x="12.333333333333364" y="448.42553191489316"><custom-block s="housekeeping"></custom-block><custom-block s="tree, level: %n size: %n"><l>9</l><l>50</l><comment w="256.66666666666663" collapsed="false">7.1.1.8.  This block differs from TREE 2 and TREE 3&#xD;in that it takes an extra input LEVEL for how many levels&#xD;to draw, and in the recursive calls that input is given a &#xD;value one less than in the current call.</comment></custom-block></script><script x="13.333333333333382" y="367.75886524822687"><custom-block s="housekeeping"></custom-block><custom-block s="tree 5, size: %n"><l>50</l><comment w="90" collapsed="true">7.1.1.7</comment></custom-block></script><script x="20.333333333333368" y="287.09219858156035"><custom-block s="housekeeping"></custom-block><custom-block s="tree 4, size: %n"><l>50</l><comment w="90" collapsed="true">7.1.1.6</comment></custom-block></script><script x="21.333333333333364" y="211.4255319148938"><custom-block s="housekeeping"></custom-block><custom-block s="tree 3, size: %n"><l>50</l><comment w="90" collapsed="true">7.1.1.5</comment></custom-block></script><comment x="15.000000000000005" y="111.09219858156025" w="385.00000000000006" collapsed="false">7.1.1.4  Position and direction of the sprite when tree 1 stops running are exactly the same as when it started drawing tree 1: SIZE steps up from the origin, facing 25 degrees left.  This is essential for tree 2 as the sprite needs to draw a second branch after drawing the first and needs to remember where it was and what direction it was facing before it started drawing the first branch. </comment><comment x="12.99999999999999" y="557.0921985815601" w="253" collapsed="false">7.1.1.9 The recursive block tree does not know when to terminate as there is no &quot;base case&quot; that tells it to stop once it reaches level 1.</comment></scripts></sprite></sprites></stage><variables></variables></scene></scenes></project>